content:
{
  "analysis": "I'm in the /workspace directory which contains backlog.json, notes.txt, gen_inputs.py, setup.sh, and a skill_context directory. I need to explore these files to understand the backlog items, team capacity, and any existing documentation before creating the product-owner package.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace by reading the key files: backlog.json, notes.txt, and checking the skill_context directory for any relevant documentation. This will help me understand the backlog items, priorities, and team capacity data.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat backlog.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat notes.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the backlog.json file contains project info for 'Atlas Analytics' with team 'North Star Squad', average_velocity of 28, availability_factor of 0.9, and a sprint goal. There are multiple user stories (US-101 through US-107 visible) with points, value, risk, effort, and priority hints. The output was truncated so I need to see the full file and explore skill_context.",
  "plan": "Let me view the complete backlog.json file and explore the skill_context directory to understand any additional requirements or context for creating the product-owner package.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat backlog.json | head -100\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find skill_context -type f -name '*.md' -o -name '*.txt' -o -name '*.json' | xargs cat 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -laR skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The output is still being truncated. I need to get the complete backlog.json content and explore the skill_context directory properly. Let me use different approaches to view the files.",
  "plan": "I'll use 'less' or redirect to a file to see the complete backlog.json, and properly explore the skill_context directory structure.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l backlog.json && cat backlog.json > /tmp/backlog_full.txt && tail -50 /tmp/backlog_full.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find skill_context -type f\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I can see the complete structure. The backlog.json has 9 user stories (US-101 to US-109). The skill_context directory contains SKILL.md, manifest.json, and reference files for sprint planning and user story templates. I need to read these to understand the required format for the product-owner package.",
  "plan": "Read the skill_context files to understand the required format and guidelines for creating the product-owner package. Then I'll create the three required documents: prioritized backlog refinement, sprint plan, and velocity summary.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sprint-planning-guide.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/user-story-templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file is quite long and was truncated. I need to read specific sections about sprint planning and backlog prioritization. Let me also read the other reference files and the notes.txt to understand what's needed.",
  "plan": "Read the specific sections of SKILL.md related to sprint planning and backlog prioritization, plus the other reference files. Also read notes.txt for any additional context.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat notes.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/sprint-planning-guide.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/references/user-story-templates.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 50 'Sprint Planning Workflow' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -A 50 'Backlog Prioritization' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "All three documents have been created successfully:\n- backlog-refinement.md (3043 bytes) - Prioritized backlog with all items ranked\n- sprint-plan.md (2743 bytes) - Sprint plan with committed (25 pts) and stretch (13 pts) items\n- velocity-summary.md (1684 bytes) - Concise velocity summary\n\nNow I need to verify the content is correct and that all markers from the original backlog are preserved.",
  "plan": "Verify the content of each document to ensure they are complete and stakeholder-ready. Check that all markers from backlog.json are included.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -60 backlog-refinement.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -50 sprint-plan.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat velocity-summary.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -c 'MARKER-' backlog-refinement.md sprint-plan.md velocity-summary.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The documents are created but I notice the date in backlog-refinement.md shows the literal string `$(date +%Y-%m-%d)` instead of being evaluated. This is because I used single quotes in the heredoc. I should fix this and also verify the sprint-plan.md content is complete.",
  "plan": "Fix the date in backlog-refinement.md to show an actual date, and verify all documents are complete and ready for stakeholders.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -i \"s/\\$(date +%Y-%m-%d)/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)/g\" backlog-refinement.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -20 backlog-refinement.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat sprint-plan.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep 'MARKER-' backlog-refinement.md | wc -l\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
